    <!-- The on-track calendar. Plain words, never a verdict: "Over plan", not "Bad day". -->
    <string name="trends_calendar_title">On track</string>
    <string name="trends_calendar_sub">Each day against your plan</string>
    <string name="trends_calendar_title_logged">Your month</string>
    <string name="trends_calendar_sub_logged">Days with something logged</string>
    <string name="trends_calendar_help_cd">How to read this</string>
    <string name="trends_calendar_help_lose">Your plan is to eat a set amount under your total burned (TDEE). That's your resting energy (BMR) plus your activity, so it shifts a little each day. On plan means the day landed close to that gap. A bit off means near it, over or under. Over plan means most of the gap closed. Eating far under your plan also shows as a bit off, because that isn't the aim either.</string>
    <string name="trends_calendar_help_gain">Your plan is to eat a set amount over your total burned (TDEE). That's your resting energy (BMR) plus your activity, so it shifts a little each day. On plan means the day landed close to that. A bit off means near it, over or under. Under plan means you ate well short of it. Going far past your plan also shows as a bit off, because that isn't the aim either.</string>
    <string name="trends_calendar_help_hold">Your plan is your daily range. On plan means the day landed inside it. A bit off means just outside it. Off plan means well outside it.</string>
    <string name="trends_calendar_help_gray">Gray days had nothing logged, were marked untracked, or haven't happened yet. Today stays gray until you wrap up the day. No single day decides much. Look at the weeks.</string>
    <string name="trends_calendar_help_logged">Each day with something logged is filled in. Gray days had nothing logged, were marked untracked, or haven't happened yet.</string>
