    <string name="trends_running_help_cd">How this is worked out</string>
    <string name="trends_running_help">Each day, what you ate is taken away from your total burned (TDEE), and the days are added up. Total burned is your resting energy (BMR) plus your activity. Both are estimates, and a watch or a formula can be off by a few hundred a day. The weight uses a rough rule of thumb, and real change is usually slower. Water can move the scale a few pounds from one day to the next, so compare this with your weight trend over weeks. Days with nothing logged, and meals without an amount, are left out.</string>

